    {
      "id": "p1",
      "text": "After the May 3 medical entrance exam, an ordinary person speaking up from Sikar sent a tip that the test was compromised. The government testing body acted on this disclosure, referring the exam staff to investigators. This led to multiple arrests, including a trusted advocate now implicated in the leak, and the annulment of the examination. A new test date was set for all affected students, giving them a second chance.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-1",
          "how-2",
          "how-3",
          "result-0",
          "result-2"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.85
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "text": "Evidence that the exam paper was leaked reached the authorities, prompting the agency whose process was compromised to take action. A referral was made for investigation into the subject matter experts involved in the exam, resulting in people being detained. The entire exam was scrapped due to the leak, but a retest is planned so students aren't unfairly burdened by the scandal.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
        "fragments": [
          "why-0",
          "how-2",
          "result-0",
          "result-1",
          "result-2"
        ],
        "channel_role": "toned"
      },
      "warnings": [],
      "fit": 0.78
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "text": "A report was made by a concerned citizen who exposed the leak, providing proof of a security breach. The testing agency handed the matter to police for a law enforcement action, leading to the accused being held. This consequence meant the major test was invalidated, but a rescheduled event on June 21 offers a fresh chance for students to take the entrance exam.",
      "source": {
        "agent_id": "The-Everyman",
